sayip-node-utils (1.0.12-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Wire SayIP into rpt.conf on install: ensure custom/rpt includes,
    functions-sayip inheritance, and phone_functions/link_functions for
    the configured node (fixes IAX/phone DTMF).
  * Do not overwrite an existing sayip.conf unless the node number changed;
    leave unrecognized existing configs alone unless force is set.
  * On node-number change, unwire functions-sayip from the previous node's
    function table before configuring the new node.
  * Stage rpt.conf rewrites and apply mode/ownership to the staged file
    before replacing, so metadata failures leave the original untouched.

 -- Jory A. Pratt, W5GLE <geekypenguin@gmail.com>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 19:05:00 -0500

sayip-node-utils (1.0.11-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix postinst never creating the systemd service: sourcing the debconf
    confmodule inside a function re-executed the script without the
    "configure" argument, silently skipping all setup. Source it once at
    top level instead.

